meta {
  name: 13. Google OAuth - Callback (manual)
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/google/callback?code=AUTH_CODE_FROM_GOOGLE&state=STATE_FROM_REDIRECT
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  code: AUTH_CODE_FROM_GOOGLE
  state: STATE_FROM_REDIRECT
}

vars:post-response {
  token: res.body.data.access_token
  refreshToken: res.body.data.refresh_token
  userId: res.body.data.user.id
}

docs {
  # Google OAuth - Callback
  
  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/auth/google/callback`
  **Auth:** None
  
  ## Description
  
  Callback endpoint that Google redirects to after the user authorizes the application.
  The server validates the `state` against Redis, exchanges the `code` for Google OIDC tokens, verifies the token claims, registers or links the user account, and issues the application's JWT access and refresh token pair.

  ## Request

  ### Query Parameters

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `code` | `string` | Yes | Authorization code issued by Google |
  | `state` | `string` | Yes | State verification token matched against Redis |

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "user": {
        "id": 1,
        "friend_code": "DR-7K9M2X8Q4P6R",
        "name": "Google User",
        "email": "user@example.com",
        "phone": null,
        "is_email_verified": true,
        "is_phone_verified": false,
        "avatar_attachment_id": null,
        "system_role": "USER",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "wallet": 0,
        "created_at": "2026-11-11T10:00:00Z"
      },
      "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs...",
      "access_token_expires_at": "2026-10-26T21:45:00Z",
      "refresh_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs...",
      "refresh_token_expires_at": "2026-11-01T21:45:00Z",
      "expires_at": "2026-10-26T21:45:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Missing code or state query parameter
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Invalid, expired, or unmatched OAuth state
  * `500 Internal Server Error` — Failed to exchange token with Google
}
